  <title>Employee info</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Payroll</gui><gui>Employee info</gui></guiseq> lists the
  contacts marked as employees. Select one to see what payroll needs to know
  about them.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>On the <gui>Employee information</gui> tab, fill in when they
    were <gui>Born</gui>, <gui>On payroll since</gui>, their <gui>Wage</gui>,
    <gui>Payments per year</gui> and <gui>Social Security number</gui>, and
    whether they are <gui>Married</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Fill in the federal and state credits and extra withholding, and
    check <gui>Exempt</gui>, <gui>Federal withholding exempt</gui> or
    <gui>State withholding exempt</gui> where they apply.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Save</gui>. <gui>Cancel</gui> puts back what was
    saved.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Each save is kept as a new record; <gui>Last updated</gui> shows when the
  current one was made.</p>

  <section id="forms">
  <title>Signed forms</title>
  <p>The <gui>Social security medicare exemption</gui>, <gui>Federal witholding
  status</gui> and <gui>State withholding status</gui> buttons keep the
  employee's signed forms. Click one to see the current form, or to scan one
  if there is none. Right click it to scan a new form in its place. The list
  under each button holds the earlier forms; double click one to see
  it.</p>
  </section>

</page>
